SUMMARY
-------
Z3 is now visible to pkg-config as version 4.13.3 (>= 4.13 requirement).

    $ pkg-config --modversion z3
    4.13.3
    $ pkg-config --cflags --libs z3
    -I/home/z/.local/include -L/home/z/.local/lib -lz3

INSTALL METHOD
--------------
apt-get could not be used (sandbox user `z` has no passwordless sudo and
sudo requires a password). Instead of a ~55 min full source build on a
2-CPU box, this task shims the already-installed system runtime library.

The base image ships Debian package `libz3-4` version **4.13.3-1**, which
provides the runtime `/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libz3.so.4` (strings
report "4.13.3.0"). Only the *-dev* artifacts were missing (headers,
libz3.so dev symlink, z3.pc). The shim supplies exactly those, under a
user-local prefix, requiring no root:

  Prefix:           $HOME/.local
  Headers (12):     $HOME/.local/include/{z3.h,z3_api.h,z3_macros.h,
                     z3_algebraic.h,z3_ast_containers.h,z3_fixedpoint.h,
                     z3_fpa.h,z3_optimization.h,z3_polynomial.h,z3_rcf.h,
                     z3_spacer.h,z3_v1.h}
                     (copied from Z3 4.13.3 source release, matching the
                     installed library's ABI)
  Dev symlink:      $HOME/.local/lib/libz3.so  -> /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libz3.so.4
                     $HOME/.local/lib/libz3.so.4 -> (same target)
  pkg-config file:  $HOME/.local/lib/pkgconfig/z3.pc  (Version: 4.13.3)

Install script:    /home/z/my-project/scripts/env/install_z3_shim.sh
Install transcript:/home/z/my-project/scripts/logs/wave0_z3.log  (harness side)

VISIBILITY FOR FUTURE WAVES
---------------------------
$HOME/.local/lib/pkgconfig is NOT on pkg-config's default search path, so
PKG_CONFIG_PATH must be set. This is handled by:

  1. /home/z/my-project/vuma/scripts/env/z3-env.sh  (source this in build tasks)
       -> exports PKG_CONFIG_PATH, LIBRARY_PATH, LD_LIBRARY_PATH
  2. $HOME/.bashrc and $HOME/.profile (appended) — interactive/login shells.

A fresh login shell reports `pkg-config --modversion z3` -> 4.13.3 with no
extra env required.

